File Index

/useAccountModal.ts
Purpose: Phase D — Account modal's state/actions: login (awaits gameSso.startLogin's popup and maps its LoginOutcome to a status line, with its own `loginPending` flag kept separate from `busy` so the cloud buttons aren't affected; a subscribeToToken subscription flips isLoggedIn the moment the popup writes, since nothing in this window re-runs on its own), logout (local token clear only), and save/load-to-cloud for the CURRENT connection's scripts + plugins via cloudSync.ts. Save reads through UserScriptRuntime's public loadScriptsFromStorage/getStorageKey (no private-API reach); Load writes localStorage directly for both scripts and the global plugins key, then does a full page reload rather than trying to live-patch every derived runtime/plugin-host state — deliberately simpler and safer for a destructive, user-confirmed action. Phase E folded librarySync.ts's saveLibraryToCloud/loadLibraryFromCloud into the same Promise.all pair — unlike scripts/plugins, Load MERGES library content (never deletes local writings), so the confirm-dialog copy was reworded to say so accurately. Autoleveling redesign step 12 added a fifth leg the same way: autoleveling-user-data.ts's exportAll()/importRecords() round-trip through cloudSync.saveAutolevelUserData/loadAutolevelUserData — Save reads exportAll() before the Promise.all (its own await, not parallelized, since the others don't need it first), Load calls importRecords() on the fetched array right after the error checks; this is a MERGE like library content (importRecords is last-writer-wins by updatedAt), not a replace.

/useAutoLeveling.ts
Purpose: Owns the persisted `AutoLevelConfig` (per-connection localStorage) and the `AutoLevelingEngine`'s lifetime — (re)creates/binds/unbinds the engine on `connectionId` change, tracks `socketReady` off the game socket's open/close events (gates Start), and exposes `runState`/`xpProgress` plus start/stop/pause/resume/resetToDefaults/moveNext/movePrev/rescanRoom, all also reachable via `shatteredarchive:autoleveling-*` window events for external UI (compass etc). The hook owns config persistence + engine lifetime; the engine (autoleveling-engine.ts) owns all runtime behavior. Wires two `EngineDeps` added 2026-09 for live-playtest fixes: `getLearnedCooldown`/`onAbilityCooldownLearned` (bumpLearnedCooldown) round-trip the per-ability auto-tuned cooldown store in autoleveling-user-data.ts; `sendThroughCommandProcessor` routes rest commands through `RuntimeSingleton.Runtime.executeAlias` (falling back to the raw `shatteredarchive:send-command` event if no Runtime is bound) — the same alias-expansion path `useGameCommand.ts` uses for manually-typed terminal input, so a rest sequence built as the player's own alias/macro actually expands instead of being sent to the MUD verbatim.

/useAuthCallback.ts
Purpose: Phase D — on mount, reads window.location.hash for the game-sso hand-off's result (features/auth/authFragment.ts's parseAuthFragment), stores a successful token via authTokenStore, then strips the fragment via history.replaceState so it never lingers in browser history. No router exists in this app, so this runs as a plain effect from MainContainer rather than a dedicated callback route. NOT the live path since the popup rewrite (2026-07-31) — src/auth-callback.ts handles the hand-off now. Kept as the safety net for a hand-off whose returnUrl still points at the app itself: an attempt already in flight across the deploy, or an old bookmarked link. Do not "clean up" without checking for those.
